homelab-common (0.1.43) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Homelab::Common::DB::Database: a one-method Mojo::Pg::Database subclass set
    as the database_class of every runtime_pg handle, to end the runaway
    "connection not open" log flood (post-cutover #110). Mojo::Pg 4.28's _watch
    probes a backend with pg_ready while RaiseError is on; when a Patroni leader
    switch drops the connection mid async query, pg_ready dies, the reactor
    callback leaves `waiting` set and never unwatches, and the dead socket
    re-fires the callback every tick forever (~500 lines/s, 2 GB/day; it filled
    prod-homelab12). The override probes readiness safely: a dead connection
    fails the pending query once, unwatches, and drops the handle so the pool
    reconnects on the next ->db; a normal in-flight query is untouched.
    t/db-watch.t. Only homelab-api runs async query_p today, so it is the one
    tier that must restart to pick this up; other services load the (inert for
    them) class at their next restart.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 23:55:00 -0600

homelab-common (0.1.42) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Two unit drop-ins for the containers (post-cutover #108): netplan-configure
    is skipped in containers (ConditionVirtualization=!container -- it has no
    netplan configuration to apply there and its "udevadm control --reload"
    fails without udev), and systemd-networkd-wait-online runs through
    /usr/bin/homelab-wait-online, which adds --any inside a container (links
    Proxmox attaches disconnected never get carrier, so the stock wait took its
    full two minutes at every container boot, failed, and held every service
    after network-online.target for as long). VMs keep both stock units. The
    postinst clears the two units' failed state on install. t/wait-online.t.
    No Perl library changes: nothing needs a restart after this upgrade.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:30:00 -0600

homelab-common (0.1.41) unstable; urgency=medium

  * /etc/logrotate.d/00-homelab-maxsize: `maxsize 200M` as the default for
    every logrotate stanza on the host (logrotate reads the directory in name
    order; a directive outside a stanza applies to the stanzas after it). A
    log past 200 MB rotates at the next daily run whatever its schedule; the
    stock weekly rsyslog stanza let two uncompressed weeks of a flooded
    mail.log and syslog fill prod-homelab39's root disk (post-cutover #105).
    No Perl changes: nothing needs a restart after this upgrade.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0600

homelab-common (0.1.40) unstable; urgency=medium

  * homelab-mount-retry calls systemctl without a shell: a mount unit named
    with \x2d (var-lib-homelab-drive\x2dstorage.mount) was mangled by sh and
    never started, so a drive VM whose store was away at boot stayed down
    (found by the phase 1 proof on vm67, post-cutover #41 H).

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:30:00 -0600

