homelab-common (0.1.38) unstable; urgency=medium

  * homelab-mount-retry + timer: for two hours after boot, every two
    minutes, start an NFS mount that is not there and a service bound to it
    that has never been active this boot (lists in
    /etc/homelab/boot-mounts.d/, written by the mount orchestrators).
  * load_config forces server.pid_file into the unit's RuntimeDirectory when
    systemd exports one, so a pid file left on disk by a power cut is never
    read again (post-cutover #41 H, J).

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:30:00 -0600

homelab-common (0.1.37) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Mailer: send_mail takes `calendar => { method, ics }` for an iTIP message
    (homelab-calendar's invitations, post-cutover #85): multipart/mixed of a
    multipart/alternative (text/plain [+ html] + text/calendar; method=...)
    and the .ics attached, the shape every mail program's Yes/Maybe/No
    buttons are tuned to; and `reply_to`. A Subject with non-ASCII is now an
    RFC 2047 encoded word (ASCII subjects are byte-identical to before).

 -- Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>  Sat, 15 Nov 2026 10:00:00 -0600

